{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1029447-rite-of-caern-building","id":1029447,"title":"Rite of Caern Building","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-09T20:21:07-08:00","id":1029447,"title":"Rite of Caern Building","content":"I was just curious how many people used Rite of Caern Building in a game and what were your experiences with the rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T06:03:25-08:00","id":1029572,"title":"","content":"It's frequently the climax of the first year or so of plot of Werewolf LARPs. Mechanically speaking, it never worked in tabletop, but I think they fixed it for W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:34:33-08:00","id":1029762,"title":"","content":"Same as Etherial, I have used it to cap off my first chapters to a chronicle 2 or 3 times. Its a huge renown boost so it normally gets them over the hump to their 2nd rank or very close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T17:16:22-08:00","id":1029835,"title":"","content":"I've played in a few games where it was part of the story, mostly it's been shoe horned in and it all goes well and hooray level 5 Caern!<br /> <br /> Which is awesome, but not very realistic in game mechanic terms, or even in the essence of the game itself. It's supposed to be epically difficult to even make a level 1 caern.<br /> <br /> I've run two games where creating a Caern was the focus of a story for new characters.<br /> <br /> It's a great reason why different types and different tribes of garou might turn up to help. It's bringing into the world a place blessed by Gaia, a place of strength for the Nation, and a great opportunity for young Garou to get renown and possibly find and form a pack. Which makes them look even better in the eyes of their elders.<br /> <br /> First time I used it, the roll wasnt enough...so I activated ST powers and cheated and made it a Level 2 Caern rather than have it fail. I sensed the players werent ready for that possibility. Which I realised was my fault, I should have readied them for that possibility.<br /> <br /> The second time was two years ago, with a troupe of new players to the game itself. I used 8 months of weekly games to introduce them to seeing as many aspects of the Nation and garou life on Sept so they could interact and learn while playing and occasionally going on missions to clean up the area and take out local infestations of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> This time I prepared this group for failure, and said what ever the dice do is what will happen. It could botch, it could fail, they could end up dead, burn all their gnosis and battle enemies for at least 8 hours only to end up with a level 1 caern...or nothing.<br /> <br /> The rite and battle took 4 sessions to complete at the end of it. Had over 70 npcs in play that were co-ordinated and I told their triumphs and losses during the battle too. Garou, Kinfolk and Spirits.<br /> <br /> Ended up with a legitimate level 3 Caern! A few of the rolls were incredible, best ive ever rolled for anything.<br /> <br /> But....at the end...not enough gnosis. So I decided Gaia would accept Health as Gnosis. I worked out how much was still needed and split it between who was left. Everyone...everyone but the Rite Master died. As in, they then went over their health chart in sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Every player accepted it, they were gutted, but happy the Caern got to live and their sacrifice meant something. <br /> <br /> Then I had Gaia bring them all back. Each one of them healing just enough to come back from it, each garou involved received a deep scar representing the Caern itself. A mark of pride and accomplishment now as they identify with every npc who bears the same scar on much greater level of respect.<br /> <br /> Game is still going. Characters still carry the mark with pride and are now Adren and kicking some butt in the Amazon now on behalf of their home Caern in the hopes of making caern and Ranch Apocalypse allies there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T05:56:52-08:00","id":1030531,"title":"","content":"I have used it a few times and almost always as the end of a chronicle.<br /> \u200bMy Generations chronicle started in the Dark Ages and the first story ended with the creation of a new Caern after the old one was defiled and destroyed by a Vampire. The Pack survived the attack one of a few survivors actually and were refugees along with the surviving human kin trying to shelter the kin until a new home could be found. The end of the first arc was the Rite of Caern Building on an island in the Adriatic sea.<br /> \u200bThe other chronicle I used it for an ending well it didn't work out so well for the players. The Theurge leading the rite failed a few roles, The wyrm forces won a few intiative rolls and snowballed into the defenders falling one by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}